# LF in the working tree on every platform. Windows checkouts default to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite the `#!/bin/sh` shim and risk making
# a fresh CI checkout look dirty to install.ts's clean-tree gate.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures are evidence: git must not touch a byte. `text=auto` above would
# normalize line endings inside one, silently, between the test that passed on
# the working file and the bytes that landed in the commit — a path recorded
# with a CR in it is enough. Borrowed from ccc, which lost 60 KB of a recorded
# stream to exactly this and only noticed because the replay went blank
# (2026-09-02).
test/fixtures/** -text
